@kksligh thanks for reporting the issue.

What do you see happening in the interface of the router itself (under ADVANCED > Security > Access Control) when you toggle the switch in HomeAssistant?
What happens if you block the device through the interface of the router, do you see the state change in HomeAssistant?

@kksligh I just tested with a Orbi RBR750 and the "allowed on network" switch works fine for that model.
It is true that if you switch it from ON to OFF, initially it switches back to ON because the router takes quite a while to apply the change. But if you wait for like 1 minute, the switch will go to the OFF position and the device will be blocked.

Note that the "Turn on acces control" needs to be enabled in the router settings itself.
